Restore normal-mode victory logging in the run history (late.sh door hosting;
applied by the Dockerfile brogue-build stage, re-verify on CE bumps).

Upstream 1.15.1 has the victory-path condition inverted: the death path skips
Easy and Wizard games (`mode != GAME_MODE_EASY && mode != GAME_MODE_WIZARD`),
but the victory path tests `mode != GAME_MODE_NORMAL`, so ordinary victories
never reach the run history file while wizard-mode victories do. The late.sh
award pipe reads that file for the Escaped/Mastered badge pair, so the fix
matters twice over: normal wins must land, and wizard wins must not.

--- a/src/brogue/RogueMain.c
+++ b/src/brogue/RogueMain.c
@@ -1373,7 +1373,7 @@
         notifyEvent(GAMEOVER_RECORDING, 0, 0, "recording ended", "none");
     }

-    if (!rogue.playbackMode && rogue.mode != GAME_MODE_EASY && rogue.mode != GAME_MODE_NORMAL) {
+    if (!rogue.playbackMode && rogue.mode != GAME_MODE_EASY && rogue.mode != GAME_MODE_WIZARD) {
         saveRunHistory(victoryVerb, "-", (int) theEntry.score, gemCount);
     }

